# EMPLOYEE 73 — PLATFORM API GOVERNANCE, INTEGRATION GATEWAY & DEVELOPER ECOSYSTEM BACKEND

Implement a production-grade API Governance, Integration Gateway, and Developer Ecosystem backend directly in the existing Radar Tehran repository.

This is an implementation task, not an audit, review, proposal, or architecture report.

Modify the existing codebase. Build functional persistence models, services, APIs, authorization policies, administrative interfaces, integration workflows, automated tests, and operational controls.

The platform must support secure first-party and approved third-party integrations while preserving tenant isolation, backward compatibility, data governance, legal compliance, and operational reliability.

Reuse all existing infrastructure and capabilities from Employees 53–72, including authentication, RBAC, organizations, listings, transactions, financial ledger, billing, documents, audit, event processing, notifications, scheduling, search, ingestion, risk detection, compliance, legal holds, and retention precedence.

Do not introduce duplicate authentication, authorization, billing, payment, event bus, webhook engine, scheduler, rate limiter, telemetry, audit, document storage, or case-management systems.

